            "summary": "First, if we're going to jump on this bandwagon of “everything belongs to everyone”, France, Germany, etc, all these super progressive eco-friendly European nations... should immediately eliminate VISA requirements to Brazilians wanting to travel…",
            "html": "<article id=\"post-26410\" class=\"post-26410 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-english category-textos tag-amazon tag-bolsonaro tag-brazil tag-conservative tag-france tag-hypocrisy tag-imperialism tag-liberal tag-macron tag-sovereignty tag-virtue-signaling\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span class=\"cat-links\"><a href=\"cat.html#english\" rel=\"category\">English</a>, <a href=\"cat.html#textos\" rel=\"category\">Textos</a></span></div><h1 class=\"entry-title\"><a href=\"reader.html#2019-08-27-amazon-brazil-france-imperialism-and-a-telling-about-virtue-signaling.html\" rel=\"bookmark\">Amazon, Brazil, France, Imperialism and a Telling about Virtue-Signaling</a></h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span class=\"entry-date\"><a href=\"reader.html#2019-08-27-amazon-brazil-france-imperialism-and-a-telling-about-virtue-signaling.html\" rel=\"bookmark\"><time class=\"entry-date\" datetime=\"2019-08-27T14:55:47-03:00\">27/08/2019</time></a></span> <span class=\"byline\"><span class=\"author vcard\"><a class=\"url fn n\" href=\"/\" rel=\"author\">estranhosidade</a></span></span> <span class=\"comments-link\"><a href=\"reader.html#2019-08-27-amazon-brazil-france-imperialism-and-a-telling-about-virtue-signaling.html#respond\">Deixe um comentário</a></span></div><div class=\"entry-meta tag-links-top\"><span class=\"tag-links\"><a href=\"tag.html#amazon\" rel=\"tag\">Amazon</a> <a href=\"tag.html#bolsonaro\" rel=\"tag\">Bolsonaro</a> <a href=\"tag.html#brazil\" rel=\"tag\">Brazil</a> <a href=\"tag.html#conservative\" rel=\"tag\">Conservative</a> <a href=\"tag.html#france\" rel=\"tag\">France</a> <a href=\"tag.html#hypocrisy\" rel=\"tag\">Hypocrisy</a> <a href=\"tag.html#imperialism\" rel=\"tag\">Imperialism</a> <a href=\"tag.html#liberal\" rel=\"tag\">Liberal</a> <a href=\"tag.html#macron\" rel=\"tag\">Macron</a> <a href=\"tag.html#sovereignty\" rel=\"tag\">Sovereignty</a> <a href=\"tag.html#virtue-signaling\" rel=\"tag\">Virtue-Signaling</a> </span><span class=\"tag-ellipsis\" style=\"display: none;\">...</span></div></header><!-- .entry-header --><div class=\"entry-content\"><p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-26429\" src=\"https://estranhosidade.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/br9mfwcf0q101.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"474\" height=\"332\" /><br />\nFirst, if we&#8217;re going to jump on this bandwagon of <em><a href=\"https://twitter.com/emmanuelmacron/status/1164617008962527232\">“everything belongs to everyone”</a></em>, France, Germany, etc, all these super progressive eco-friendly European nations&#8230; should immediately eliminate <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20190827173846/https://www.gazetadopovo.com.br/turismo/europa-vai-exigir-autorizacao-de-viagens-de-brasileiros/\">VISA requirements to Brazilians wanting to travel or live there</a>.</p>\n<p>Second, the liberal media, as well as a big chunk of the international community, are only giving all this emphasis on this story because they don&#8217;t like Bolsonaro <em><a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/https://www1.folha.uol.com.br/ambiente/2019/08/macron-usa-foto-antiga-para-falar-de-queimadas-sob-bolsonaro.shtml\">(Macron went as far as sharing photos from 2003, when the country was still governed by the liberals)</a>,</em> and because it makes European liberals seem “woke”. In the last three years <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brumadinho_dam_disaster\">2 huge tailings dams collapsed</a> and about 300 people died, rivers were contaminated and ecosystems were destroyed – there are currently hundreds of dams in the same situation that can collapse at any moment, but you don&#8217;t see the media giving the same attention to it, because dams are not <em>“fashionable”</em> in liberal circle-jerks at the moment.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<h4>“The result is a society that pays way too much attention and gives way too much importance to what teenagers – that oftentimes cannot even fix the countless problems with their lives, problems much more important than some (realistically unreachable) far-off-their-control persute – <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20190830202435/https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/28/nyregion/greta-thunberg-new-york.html\">have to say about the world, about how we should save the planet and so on</a>. A society rooted in the <span style=\"text-decoration:underline;\">signalization of virtue</span><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;\">, </span><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;\">hypocrisy</span> and empty TED Talk&#8217;s speechs.”</h4>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Third, I would bet that most foreigners who are renting on social media about <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2019_Amazon_rainforest_wildfires\">what is happening in what is to them the other side of the world</a>, in a set of circumstances that they themselves individually can do nothing about, when it comes down to the things that they actually can do something (<em>like not throwing garbage on their streets, or not buying iPhones made in China, the most polluting country in the world)</em>, they don&#8217;t care, cause you don&#8217;t win the same “woke” points by doing these things. <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20190827072208/https://www.esquire.com/entertainment/a28797636/amazon-rainforest-fires-brazil-celebrity-reaction/\">It&#8217;s purely a virtue-signaling thing</a><em>, </em>it&#8217;s the mindset of <em>&#8220;look at me, look at how I&#8217;m such a good person, adore me!”, </em>it is slacktivism in a nutshell – which is very well illustrated on this <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qTk-69f64KU\">Jordan Peterson&#8217;s video</a>.</p>\n<p>And lastly, <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20190827072411/https://noticias.uol.com.br/meio-ambiente/ultimas-noticias/redacao/2019/08/22/general-villas-boas-questiona-autoridade-moral-da-franca-sobre-queimadas.htm\">for a country that tested nuclear weapons in fishing villages</a>, an event that still today produces consequences to the native islanders, a country that cut down almost all its original forests and so on, France should really think twice before going around pointing fingers at others.</p>\n</div></article>",
